  "limitations": [
    "The host must hold exclusive native-write ownership of enrolled private handles and preinvalidate before every raw or legacy SQL dispatch. Arbitrary SQL on an enrolled context is not automatically intercepted.",
    "Activation must be submitted as a standalone trusted command. The probe rejects a persistent mutation in its own activation transaction, but it does not certify a host multi-statement dispatch envelope spanning separate transactions.",
    "The audit covers canonical retained assertion carriers, intervals, and entity-history bindings. It does not certify every receipt, clock value, or storage-usage counter.",
    "The owner state is volatile and scoped to the actual DatabaseInstance and context lifecycle. A reopened instance must enroll and audit again.",
    "Cancellation is forwarded while the internal query task loop runs and checked before publication. Query submission and any individual native task may still delay interrupt observation.",
    "The worker core artifact uses its existing 0.18.0 build metadata plus the approved shared integrity extraction and root command-capacity source. It is distinct from the integration branch 0.19 artifact.",
    "The optional companion and focused activation suite are not part of the default build or verification. No production fast-read validation bypass is implemented."
  ],
  "review": {
    "reviewer_role": "independent orchestration operations agent",
    "result": "No new blocker after source review of pending task cancellation, deferred enrollment, generation fencing, and clean QueryEnd publication. Standalone trusted activation and preinvalidate raw-dispatch host contract required."
  }
